{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ADrkdgYzuVcEKfRH4FwKzq","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"attavo frontier: the waves, built by the product.\n2\t\n3\tThree reads, nothing written. The plan's latest version in the store\n4\t(attavo/plan.py) gives the order: epic rank, then issue rank within the\n5\tepic; an open issue the plan does not place is Backlog, last, by number.\n6\tThe tenant's issues through [forge].issues_command (attavo/issues.py)\n7\tgive each issue's state, class and, before it has a spec, its Claims.\n8\tWork in flight from git (attavo/claims.py) gives wave 0.\n9\t\n10\tWave 0 is the work holding claims now: every branch not on the default\n11\tbranch, with the paths it declares and changes. Wave 1 walks the order\n12\tand places each open issue whose predecessors (its depends and ruled\n13\tedges) are closed or placed in an earlier wave, whose Claims overlap no\n14\tclaim already placed in the wave, none still held in wave 0, and -- strict\n15\topportunism (ruled 2026-09-29) -- none of an open issue ranked above it\n16\tthat is not yet placed, ready or not: a lower-ranked issue never takes a\n17\tpath a higher-ranked one wants. Wave k+1 walks what is left as if the\n18\twaves before it had merged. Overlap is attavo.claims.overlap, the\n19\tproduct's only rule. An issue with no Claims is not placed: nothing shows\n20\tit disjoint from anything. Every placed issue carries a why line for each\n21\treason it waited; wave 1's say nothing. The output has no dates: waves\n22\tare an order, not a forecast.\n23\t\n24\tEpic progress is closed issues over all issues under the epic, as the\n25\tforge reports them, never typed.\n26\t\"\"\"\n27\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n28\t\n29\timport json\n30\timport re\n31\timport sys\n32\timport tempfile\n33\tfrom pathlib import Path\n34\tfrom typing import Any\n35\t\n36\tfrom attavo import store\n37\tfrom attavo.claims import ITEM_BRANCH, _git, default_branch, in_flight, overlap\n38\tfrom attavo.common import MANIFEST, read_manifest\n39\tfrom attavo.issues import Issue, read_issues\n40\tfrom attavo.plan import BACKLOG, DOC\n41\tfrom attavo.records import RecordItemMismatch, _load_record\n42\t\n43\tORDER = (\"epic rank, then issue rank within the epic; an open issue the plan does not place \"\n44\t         \"is Backlog, last, by number\")\n45\tRECORD = re.compile(r\"^(spec|approval|build|verify)-([0-9]{2,})\\.(json|started)$\")\n46\t\n47\t\n48\tdef _overlaps(mine: list[str], theirs: list[str]) -> list[str]:\n49\t    return sorted({t for t in theirs for c in mine if overlap(c, t)} |\n50\t                  {c for c in mine for t in theirs if overlap(c, t)})\n51\t\n52\t\n53\tdef branch_state(root: Path, ref: str, records_rel: str, item: str | None) -> str:\n54\t    \"\"\"Where an item branch stands, from the records it carries: \"spec\n55\t    pushed\" (no gate record yet), \"spec refused\", \"awaiting approval\",\n56\t    \"approved\", \"building\", \"in review\". A branch with no item says\n57\t    \"lane\".\"\"\"\n58\t    if item is None:\n59\t        return \"lane\"\n60\t    listed = _git(root, \"ls-tree\", \"--name-only\", f\"{ref}:{records_rel}/{item}\").stdout.split()\n61\t    seen: dict[str, list[int]] = {}\n62\t    for name in listed:\n63\t        mm = RECORD.match(name)\n64\t        if mm:\n65\t            seen.setdefault(mm.group(1), []).append(int(mm.group(2)))\n66\t    if \"verify\" in seen:\n67\t        return \"in review\"\n68\t    if \"build\" in seen:\n69\t        return \"building\"\n70\t    if \"approval\" in seen:\n71\t        return \"approved\"\n72\t    if \"spec\" not in seen:\n73\t        return \"spec pushed\"\n74\t    name = f\"spec-{max(seen['spec']):02d}.json\"\n75\t    text = _git(root, \"show\", f\"{ref}:{records_rel}/{item}/{name}\").stdout\n76\t    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as tmp:\n77\t        path = Path(tmp) / item / name\n78\t        path.parent.mkdir()\n79\t        path.write_text(text)\n80\t        try:\n81\t            status = _load_record(path, item).get(\"status\")\n82\t        except (ValueError, RecordItemMismatch):\n83\t            status = None\n84\t    return \"awaiting approval\" if status == \"pass\" else \"spec refused\"\n85\t\n86\t\n87\tdef compute(body: dict[str, Any], issues: list[Issue], flights: list[dict[str, Any]],\n88\t            states: dict[str, str] | None = None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n89\t    \"\"\"The waves and epic progress, from the plan, the issues and the\n90\t    work in flight. Pure: the reads are the caller's.\"\"\"\n91\t    states = states or {}\n92\t    by_number = {i[\"number\"]: i for i in issues}\n93\t    epic_of: dict[int, str] = {}\n94\t    order: list[int] = []\n95\t    for e in body[\"epics\"]:\n96\t        for n in e[\"issues\"]:\n97\t            epic_of[n] = e[\"id\"]\n98\t            order.append(n)\n99\t    unplaced = sorted(n for n, i in by_number.items() if i[\"state\"] == \"open\" and n not in epic_of)\n100\t    for n in unplaced:\n101\t        epic_of[n] = BACKLOG\n102\t    backlog_at = next((k for k, e in enumerate(body[\"epics\"]) if e[\"id\"] == BACKLOG), len(body[\"epics\"]))\n103\t    rank: list[int] = []\n104\t    for k, e in enumerate(body[\"epics\"]):\n105\t        rank += e[\"issues\"]\n106\t        if k == backlog_at:\n107\t            rank += unplaced\n108\t    preds: dict[int, list[tuple[int, str]]] = {}\n109\t    for g in body.get(\"edges\", []):\n110\t        preds.setdefault(g[\"to\"], []).append((g[\"from\"], g[\"type\"]))\n111\t\n112\t    def title(n: int) -> str:\n113\t        return by_number[n][\"title\"] if n in by_number else f\"#{n} (not read from the forge)\"\n114\t\n115\t    wave0: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n116\t    held: list[tuple[str, list[str]]] = []\n117\t    in_flight_items: set[int] = set()\n118\t    for f in flights:\n119\t        claims = f[\"declared\"] + [p for p in f[\"changed\"] if p not in f[\"declared\"]]\n120\t        n = int(f[\"item\"]) if f.get(\"item\") and str(f[\"item\"]).isdigit() else None\n121\t        if n is not None:\n122\t            in_flight_items.add(n)\n123\t        wave0.append({\"issue\": n, \"branch\": f[\"branch\"], \"title\": title(n) if n else f[\"branch\"],\n124\t                      \"epic\": epic_of.get(n) if n else None,\n125\t                      \"class\": by_number[n][\"item_class\"] if n in by_number else None,\n126\t                      \"claims\": claims, \"spec_state\": states.get(f[\"branch\"], \"lane\" if n is None else \"spec pushed\"),\n127\t                      \"why\": []})\n128\t        held.append((f[\"branch\"], claims))\n129\t\n130\t    def is_open(n: int) -> bool:\n131\t        return n in by_number and by_number[n][\"state\"] == \"open\"\n132\t\n133\t    remaining = [n for n in rank if is_open(n) and n not in in_flight_items]\n134\t    placed_wave: dict[int, int] = {n: 0 for n in in_flight_items}\n135\t    not_placed: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n136\t    why: dict[int, list[str]] = {}\n137\t\n138\t    def note(n: int, line: str) -> None:\n139\t        why.setdefault(n, [])\n140\t        if line not in why[n]:\n141\t            why[n].append(line)\n142\t\n143\t    for n in list(remaining):\n144\t        if by_number[n][\"claims\"] is None:\n145\t            not_placed.append({\"issue\": n, \"title\": title(n), \"epic\": epic_of[n],\n146\t                               \"why\": [\"no claims: the issue has no Claims section and no spec\"]})\n147\t            remaining.remove(n)\n148\t\n149\t    waves: list[list[dict[str, Any]]] = [wave0]\n150\t    k = 0\n151\t    while remaining:\n152\t        k += 1\n153\t        this_wave: list[tuple[int, list[str]]] = []\n154\t        progressed = False\n155\t        for idx, n in enumerate(remaining):\n156\t            mine = by_number[n][\"claims\"] or []\n157\t            blocked = False\n158\t            for p, kind in preds.get(n, []):\n159\t                if p in by_number and by_number[p][\"state\"] == \"closed\":\n160\t                    continue\n161\t                if placed_wave.get(p, k) < k:\n162\t                    continue\n163\t                note(n, f\"waits on #{p} ({kind})\")\n164\t                blocked = True\n165\t            if k == 1:\n166\t                for branch, claims in held:\n167\t                    hit = _overlaps(mine, claims)\n168\t                    if hit:\n169\t                        note(n, f\"waits on branch {branch}: {', '.join(hit)}\")\n170\t                        blocked = True\n171\t            for m, claims in this_wave:\n172\t                hit = _overlaps(mine, claims)\n173\t                if hit:\n174\t                    note(n, f\"shares {', '.join(hit)} with #{m} in wave {k}\")\n175\t                    blocked = True\n176\t            for m in remaining[:idx]:\n177\t                if placed_wave.get(m) is not None:\n178\t                    continue\n179\t                hit = _overlaps(mine, by_number[m][\"claims\"] or [])\n180\t                if hit:\n181\t                    note(n, f\"yields {', '.join(hit)} to #{m}, ranked above\")\n182\t                    blocked = True\n183\t            if not blocked:\n184\t                this_wave.append((n, mine))\n185\t                placed_wave[n] = k\n186\t                progressed = True\n187\t        if not progressed and k == 1 and held:\n188\t            # Nothing can start while the work in flight holds its paths;\n189\t            # wave 2 reads as if that work had merged. An empty wave 1 says so.\n190\t            waves.append([])\n191\t            continue\n192\t        if not progressed:\n193\t            for n in remaining:\n194\t                not_placed.append({\"issue\": n, \"title\": title(n), \"epic\": epic_of[n],\n195\t                                   \"why\": why.get(n) or [\"cannot be ordered: its predecessors are never placed\"]})\n196\t            break\n197\t        waves.append([{\"issue\": n, \"title\": title(n), \"epic\": epic_of[n],\n198\t                       \"class\": by_number[n][\"item_class\"], \"claims\": claims,\n199\t                       \"spec_state\": \"no spec\", \"why\": why.get(n, []) if k > 1 else []}\n200\t                      for n, claims in this_wave])\n201\t        remaining = [n for n in remaining if n not in placed_wave]\n202\t\n203\t    epics = []\n204\t    for e in body[\"epics\"]:\n205\t        members = list(e[\"issues\"]) + (unplaced if e[\"id\"] == BACKLOG else [])\n206\t        known = [n for n in members if n in by_number]\n207\t        epics.append({\"id\": e[\"id\"], \"title\": e[\"title\"],\n208\t                      \"closed\": sum(1 for n in known if by_number[n][\"state\"] == \"closed\"),\n209\t                      \"total\": len(known)})\n210\t    return {\"order\": ORDER, \"epics\": epics, \"waves\": waves, \"not_placed\": not_placed}\n211\t\n212\t\n213\tdef cmd_frontier(argv: list[str]) -> int:\n214\t    as_json = \"--json\" in argv\n215\t    root = Path(\".\").resolve()\n216\t    m = read_manifest(root)\n217\t    if m is None:\n218\t        print(f\"attavo frontier: no {MANIFEST} at {root}\", file=sys.stderr)\n219\t        return 2\n220\t    default = default_branch(root)\n221\t    if default is None:\n222\t        print(\"attavo frontier: refused: refs/remotes/origin/HEAD is not set; \"\n223\t              \"run `git remote set-head origin -a`\", file=sys.stderr)\n224\t        return 2\n225\t    try:\n226\t        env = store.get(root, DOC)\n227\t    except store.StoreRefusal as r:\n228\t        print(f\"attavo frontier: not read: {r}\", file=sys.stderr)\n229\t        return 2\n230\t    if env is None:\n231\t        print(\"attavo frontier: not read: no plan in the store\", file=sys.stderr)\n232\t        return 2\n233\t    issues, why = read_issues(root, m)\n234\t    if issues is None:\n235\t        print(f\"attavo frontier: {why}\", file=sys.stderr)\n236\t        return 2\n237\t    flights = in_flight(root, m, default)\n238\t    records_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"records\"].strip(\"/\")\n239\t    states = {f[\"branch\"]: branch_state(root, f\"refs/remotes/origin/{f['branch']}\", records_rel,\n240\t                                        f[\"item\"] if f.get(\"item\") and ITEM_BRANCH.match(f[\"branch\"]) else None)\n241\t              for f in flights}\n242\t    out = compute(env[\"body\"], issues, flights, states)\n243\t    out = {\"default\": default, \"plan_version\": env[\"version\"], **out}\n244\t    if as_json:\n245\t        print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n246\t        return 0\n247\t    print(f\"frontier against {default[len('refs/remotes/'):]}, plan version {env['version']}; order: {out['order']}\")\n248\t    for e in out[\"epics\"]:\n249\t        print(f\"  {e['id']}: {e['closed']} of {e['total']} closed - {e['title']}\")\n250\t    for k, wave in enumerate(out[\"waves\"]):\n251\t        print(f\"wave {k}{' (in flight)' if k == 0 else ''}: {len(wave)}\")\n252\t        for x in wave:\n253\t            label = f\"#{x['issue']}\" if x[\"issue\"] else x.get(\"branch\", \"\")\n254\t            print(f\"  {label} [{x['spec_state']}] {x['title']}\")\n255\t            for line in x[\"why\"]:\n256\t                print(f\"      {line}\")\n257\t    if out[\"not_placed\"]:\n258\t        print(f\"not placed: {len(out['not_placed'])}\")\n259\t        for x in out[\"not_placed\"]:\n260\t            print(f\"  #{x['issue']} {x['title']}: {'; '.join(x['why'])}\")\n261\t    return 0\n262\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4588db83-1ef4-4bee-8419-3aef77f32fac","uuid":"c8b6de42-30cc-41b9-b2fd-71ef529456ff","timestamp":"2026-09-30T02:29:23.947Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-281/attest/specs/281/stub/attavo/frontier.py","content":"\"\"\"attavo frontier: the waves, built by the product.\n\nThree reads, nothing written. The plan's latest version in the store\n(attavo/plan.py) gives the order: epic rank, then issue rank within the\nepic; an open issue the plan does not place is Backlog, last, by number.\nThe tenant's issues through [forge].issues_command (attavo/issues.py)\ngive each issue's state, class and, before it has a spec, its Claims.\nWork in flight from git (attavo/claims.py) gives wave 0.\n\nWave 0 is the work holding claims now: every branch not on the default\nbranch, with the paths it declares and changes. Wave 1 walks the order\nand places each open issue whose predecessors (its depends and ruled\nedges) are closed or placed in an earlier wave, whose Claims overlap no\nclaim already placed in the wave, none still held in wave 0, and -- strict\nopportunism (ruled 2026-09-29) -- none of an open issue ranked above it\nthat is not yet placed, ready or not: a lower-ranked issue never takes a\npath a higher-ranked one wants. Wave k+1 walks what is left as if the\nwaves before it had merged. Overlap is attavo.claims.overlap, the\nproduct's only rule. An issue with no Claims is not placed: nothing shows\nit disjoint from anything. Every placed issue carries a why line for each\nreason it waited; wave 1's say nothing. The output has no dates: waves\nare an order, not a forecast.\n\nEpic progress is closed issues over all issues under the epic, as the\nforge reports them, never typed.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nimport re\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\n\nfrom attavo import store\nfrom attavo.claims import ITEM_BRANCH, _git, default_branch, in_flight, overlap\nfrom attavo.common import MANIFEST, read_manifest\nfrom attavo.issues import Issue, read_issues\nfrom attavo.plan import BACKLOG, DOC\nfrom attavo.records import RecordItemMismatch, _load_record\n\nORDER = (\"epic rank, then issue rank within the epic; an open issue the plan does not place \"\n         \"is Backlog, last, by number\")\nRECORD = re.compile(r\"^(spec|approval|build|verify)-([0-9]{2,})\\.(json|started)$\")\n\n\ndef _overlaps(mine: list[str], theirs: list[str]) -> list[str]:\n    return sorted({t for t in theirs for c in mine if overlap(c, t)} |\n                  {c for c in mine for t in theirs if overlap(c, t)})\n\n\ndef branch_state(root: Path, ref: str, records_rel: str, item: str | None) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Where an item branch stands, from the records it carries: \"spec\n    pushed\" (no gate record yet), \"spec refused\", \"awaiting approval\",\n    \"approved\", \"building\", \"in review\". A branch with no item says\n    \"lane\".\"\"\"\n    if item is None:\n        return \"lane\"\n    listed = _git(root, \"ls-tree\", \"--name-only\", f\"{ref}:{records_rel}/{item}\").stdout.split()\n    seen: dict[str, list[int]] = {}\n    for name in listed:\n        mm = RECORD.match(name)\n        if mm:\n            seen.setdefault(mm.group(1), []).append(int(mm.group(2)))\n    if \"verify\" in seen:\n        return \"in review\"\n    if \"build\" in seen:\n        return \"building\"\n    if \"approval\" in seen:\n        return \"approved\"\n    if \"spec\" not in seen:\n        return \"spec pushed\"\n    name = f\"spec-{max(seen['spec']):02d}.json\"\n    text = _git(root, \"show\", f\"{ref}:{records_rel}/{item}/{name}\").stdout\n    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as tmp:\n        path = Path(tmp) / item / name\n        path.parent.mkdir()\n        path.write_text(text)\n        try:\n            status = _load_record(path, item).get(\"status\")\n        except (ValueError, RecordItemMismatch):\n            status = None\n    return \"awaiting approval\" if status == \"pass\" else \"spec refused\"\n\n\ndef compute(body: dict[str, Any], issues: list[Issue], flights: list[dict[str, Any]],\n            states: dict[str, str] | None = None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"The waves and epic progress, from the plan, the issues and the\n    work in flight. Pure: the reads are the caller's.\"\"\"\n    states = states or {}\n    by_number = {i[\"number\"]: i for i in issues}\n    epic_of: dict[int, str] = {}\n    order: list[int] = []\n    for e in body[\"epics\"]:\n        for n in e[\"issues\"]:\n            epic_of[n] = e[\"id\"]\n            order.append(n)\n    unplaced = sorted(n for n, i in by_number.items() if i[\"state\"] == \"open\" and n not in epic_of)\n    for n in unplaced:\n        epic_of[n] = BACKLOG\n    backlog_at = next((k for k, e in enumerate(body[\"epics\"]) if e[\"id\"] == BACKLOG), len(body[\"epics\"]))\n    rank: list[int] = []\n    for k, e in enumerate(body[\"epics\"]):\n        rank += e[\"issues\"]\n        if k == backlog_at:\n            rank += unplaced\n    preds: dict[int, list[tuple[int, str]]] = {}\n    for g in body.get(\"edges\", []):\n        preds.setdefault(g[\"to\"], []).append((g[\"from\"], g[\"type\"]))\n\n    def title(n: int) -> str:\n        return by_number[n][\"title\"] if n in by_number else f\"#{n} (not read from the forge)\"\n\n    wave0: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n    held: list[tuple[str, list[str]]] = []\n    in_flight_items: set[int] = set()\n    for f in flights:\n        claims = f[\"declared\"] + [p for p in f[\"changed\"] if p not in f[\"declared\"]]\n        n = int(f[\"item\"]) if f.get(\"item\") and str(f[\"item\"]).isdigit() else None\n        if n is not None:\n            in_flight_items.add(n)\n        wave0.append({\"issue\": n, \"branch\": f[\"branch\"], \"title\": title(n) if n else f[\"branch\"],\n                      \"epic\": epic_of.get(n) if n else None,\n                      \"class\": by_number[n][\"item_class\"] if n in by_number else None,\n                      \"claims\": claims, \"spec_state\": states.get(f[\"branch\"], \"lane\" if n is None else \"spec pushed\"),\n                      \"why\": []})\n        held.append((f[\"branch\"], claims))\n\n    def is_open(n: int) -> bool:\n        return n in by_number and by_number[n][\"state\"] == \"open\"\n\n    remaining = [n for n in rank if is_open(n) and n not in in_flight_items]\n    placed_wave: dict[int, int] = {n: 0 for n in in_flight_items}\n    not_placed: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n    why: dict[int, list[str]] = {}\n\n    def note(n: int, line: str) -> None:\n        why.setdefault(n, [])\n        if line not in why[n]:\n            why[n].append(line)\n\n    for n in list(remaining):\n        if by_number[n][\"claims\"] is None:\n            not_placed.append({\"issue\": n, \"title\": title(n), \"epic\": epic_of[n],\n                               \"why\": [\"no claims: the issue has no Claims section and no spec\"]})\n            remaining.remove(n)\n\n    waves: list[list[dict[str, Any]]] = [wave0]\n    k = 0\n    while remaining:\n        k += 1\n        this_wave: list[tuple[int, list[str]]] = []\n        progressed = False\n        for idx, n in enumerate(remaining):\n            mine = by_number[n][\"claims\"] or []\n            blocked = False\n            for p, kind in preds.get(n, []):\n                if p in by_number and by_number[p][\"state\"] == \"closed\":\n                    continue\n                if placed_wave.get(p, k) < k:\n                    continue\n                note(n, f\"waits on #{p} ({kind})\")\n                blocked = True\n            if k == 1:\n                for branch, claims in held:\n                    hit = _overlaps(mine, claims)\n                    if hit:\n                        note(n, f\"waits on branch {branch}: {', '.join(hit)}\")\n                        blocked = True\n            for m, claims in this_wave:\n                hit = _overlaps(mine, claims)\n                if hit:\n                    note(n, f\"shares {', '.join(hit)} with #{m} in wave {k}\")\n                    blocked = True\n            for m in remaining[:idx]:\n                if placed_wave.get(m) is not None:\n                    continue\n                hit = _overlaps(mine, by_number[m][\"claims\"] or [])\n                if hit:\n                    note(n, f\"yields {', '.join(hit)} to #{m}, ranked above\")\n                    blocked = True\n            if not blocked:\n                this_wave.append((n, mine))\n                placed_wave[n] = k\n                progressed = True\n        if not progressed and k == 1 and held:\n            # Nothing can start while the work in flight holds its paths;\n            # wave 2 reads as if that work had merged. An empty wave 1 says so.\n            waves.append([])\n            continue\n        if not progressed:\n            for n in remaining:\n                not_placed.append({\"issue\": n, \"title\": title(n), \"epic\": epic_of[n],\n                                   \"why\": why.get(n) or [\"cannot be ordered: its predecessors are never placed\"]})\n            break\n        waves.append([{\"issue\": n, \"title\": title(n), \"epic\": epic_of[n],\n                       \"class\": by_number[n][\"item_class\"], \"claims\": claims,\n                       \"spec_state\": \"no spec\", \"why\": why.get(n, []) if k > 1 else []}\n                      for n, claims in this_wave])\n        remaining = [n for n in remaining if n not in placed_wave]\n\n    epics = []\n    for e in body[\"epics\"]:\n        members = list(e[\"issues\"]) + (unplaced if e[\"id\"] == BACKLOG else [])\n        known = [n for n in members if n in by_number]\n        epics.append({\"id\": e[\"id\"], \"title\": e[\"title\"],\n                      \"closed\": sum(1 for n in known if by_number[n][\"state\"] == \"closed\"),\n                      \"total\": len(known)})\n    return {\"order\": ORDER, \"epics\": epics, \"waves\": waves, \"not_placed\": not_placed}\n\n\ndef cmd_frontier(argv: list[str]) -> int:\n    as_json = \"--json\" in argv\n    root = Path(\".\").resolve()\n    m = read_manifest(root)\n    if m is None:\n        print(f\"attavo frontier: no {MANIFEST} at {root}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    default = default_branch(root)\n    if default is None:\n        print(\"attavo frontier: refused: refs/remotes/origin/HEAD is not set; \"\n              \"run `git remote set-head origin -a`\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    try:\n        env = store.get(root, DOC)\n    except store.StoreRefusal as r:\n        print(f\"attavo frontier: not read: {r}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    if env is None:\n        print(\"attavo frontier: not read: no plan in the store\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    issues, why = read_issues(root, m)\n    if issues is None:\n        print(f\"attavo frontier: {why}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    flights = in_flight(root, m, default)\n    records_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"records\"].strip(\"/\")\n    states = {f[\"branch\"]: branch_state(root, f\"refs/remotes/origin/{f['branch']}\", records_rel,\n                                        f[\"item\"] if f.get(\"item\") and ITEM_BRANCH.match(f[\"branch\"]) else None)\n              for f in flights}\n    out = compute(env[\"body\"], issues, flights, states)\n    out = {\"default\": default, \"plan_version\": env[\"version\"], **out}\n    if as_json:\n        print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n        return 0\n    print(f\"frontier against {default[len('refs/remotes/'):]}, plan version {env['version']}; order: {out['order']}\")\n    for e in out[\"epics\"]:\n        print(f\"  {e['id']}: {e['closed']} of {e['total']} closed - {e['title']}\")\n    for k, wave in enumerate(out[\"waves\"]):\n        print(f\"wave {k}{' (in flight)' if k == 0 else ''}: {len(wave)}\")\n        for x in wave:\n            label = f\"#{x['issue']}\" if x[\"issue\"] else x.get(\"branch\", \"\")\n            print(f\"  {label} [{x['spec_state']}] {x['title']}\")\n            for line in x[\"why\"]:\n                print(f\"      {line}\")\n    if out[\"not_placed\"]:\n        print(f\"not placed: {len(out['not_placed'])}\")\n        for x in out[\"not_placed\"]:\n            print(f\"  #{x['issue']} {x['title']}: {'; '.join(x['why'])}\")\n    return 0\n","numLines":262,"startLine":1,"totalLines":262}}}
